## 1. "Insecure random number generation" — routes/simulation.py  → FALSE POSITIVE
The flagged calls (random.randint / choice / uniform on lines ~202-228) are made on
`_sim_random = secrets.SystemRandom()` (see routes/simulation.py line 6), i.e. a
cryptographically-secure RNG that exposes the random.* API. No insecure `random`
module usage exists here. The module is also a demo/simulation route (fake driver
jitter), not a security-sensitive context. No change required.

